  "_notes": {
    "addslashes": "listed as TRANSPARENT on purpose: a string transformation, not a substitution by a verified element; bypassable (multibyte). Taint passes, sanitization is NOT credited.",
    "strip_tags": "transparent for the same reason: it is not an HTML escaper.",
    "transparent": "taint passes through; any sanitization already earned is DROPPED (substr of an escaped string can end in a lone backslash; stripslashes undoes escaping outright). Too strict is a verdict that can be redeemed; too lax is one that lies.",
    "preserving": "taint passes through and earned sanitization is KEPT: case changes, whitespace trimming and padding cannot create a quote or strand a backslash — after mysqli_real_escape_string no raw whitespace-escape remains to strip. ARGUED from the escaper's contract, not measured against MySQL; a counterexample moves the entry to `transparent`.",
    "_SERVER": "attacker-written entries only: HTTP_* (every request header, HTTP_HOST and HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR included), the request line and path. REMOTE_ADDR, SERVER_*, DOCUMENT_ROOT are set by the server and read as constants. A computed key is assumed hot.",
    "narrowing": "taint passes; only a NUMERIC substitution survives (digits stay digits under any cut), a context escape does not (substr can strand a backslash).",
    "explode/implode": "preserving when the delimiter is a literal without quote, backslash or NUL (it cannot strand an escape); otherwise narrowing."
  },
